# React Patterns

## Mobile-First Breakpoints Only (S1)
Use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`. **Never use `max-*` variants**.

## Named Exports (S2)
Components, hooks, and utilities use **named exports**. `src/AppRoute/index.tsx` may keep a default export because `main.tsx` imports it that way until it is refactored.

## TanStack Query for Server State (S3)
No `useEffect` + `fetch` for reads. Put `useQuery` hooks in `query.tsx` with typed query keys. Mutations in `action.tsx`.

## Single Route Registry (S4)
All routes are registered in `src/AppRoute/index.tsx` with **`createBrowserRouter`**. No scattered `<Route>` trees. Wrap each page in `RouteErrorBoundary` once that helper exists.

## Absolute Imports (S5)
`@/` for cross-folder imports. Relative `./` only inside the same component folder.

## Error Boundaries per Route (S6)
Errors in one route must not crash the app. Add `RouteErrorBoundary` when routing is expanded beyond the scaffold.

## `React.lazy` + `Suspense` per Route (S7)
New page-level components are code-split with `React.lazy` in the route registry.
